1. Add the shared-vocabulary import to .LLMDD/tools/run-waves.py, beside the existing imports at the top of the file. Sequence is already imported from typing by this module, so no typing change is needed:

```python
from cu_scope import NoTouch, is_touched, parse_no_touch
```

Prove: `python3 -m py_compile .LLMDD/tools/run-waves.py`

2. Read the no-touch set for a CU before its Coder starts. Add this helper immediately after the _COMPONENT_FILES definition near line 671, so it sits with the other CU file resolution code. Sequence and Ok and Err and typing and Path are all already available in this module:

```python
def _cu_no_touch(cu_dir: Path) -> NoTouch:
    """Return the no-touch set declared by one CU frame folder."""
    steps: Path = cu_dir / "IMPLEMENTATION_STEPS.itr"
    opened: Ok[typing.TextIO] | Err[Exception] = _open_file(steps)
    if isinstance(opened, Err):
        return parse_no_touch("")
    handle: typing.TextIO = opened.value
    text: str = handle.read()
    handle.close()
    return parse_no_touch(text)
```

Prove: `python3 -m py_compile .LLMDD/tools/run-waves.py`

